+Various heuristics assist in determining whether colors should be enabled by default. Specifically, Loguru honors |the-no-color-environment-variable|_ and disables coloring if it is set to any value (it takes precedence over ``FORCE_COLOR``). Conversely, it honors |the-force-color-environment-variable|_ and enables coloring if it is set to any value, which is useful for non-TTY environments that nevertheless support colors. Additionally, terminals identified by ``TERM=dumb`` are considered to lack color support.
 
